  "notes": "Cash basis county. Receipts/disbursements from Exhibit B (p2) Total Governmental Funds column; operating transfers (86,000 in/out) are eliminated in that column so transfers_in/out are null. Beginning and ending cash from Exhibit B continued (p3); roll-forward 1,949,044 + 1,783,283 - 2,224,975 = 1,507,352. Balance sheet is the cash-basis fund balance section of Exhibit B continued (no liabilities). Taxes on Exhibit B (966,493): the Inheritance Fund column's 77,003 is split out as inheritance tax (split_from); the remaining 889,490 stays taxes (unlabeled) because Exhibit A general receipts taxes (1,089,831) do not tie to it. Detail: General Fund (Schedule 3, pp5-8) lines with blank actuals (Zoning, Jail, Elections capital outlay, Weed Control operating, Misc capital, Board supplies) are zero and omitted; budget_final holds the printed Original Budget (or Budget) column. General Fund Public Works (noxious weed 33,874) and Veterans (7,560) categorized by function; Miscellaneous - general is counted under general government per Exhibit B (606,196 = 486,221 + 119,975). Road Sinking Fund (Schedule 5) has only a 46,000 transfer in; its capital outlay actual is blank. Schedule 1 (nonmajor funds, p4) recorded from its Total column (more than 6 funds). Transfer cross-check: General out 40,000 and Road and Bridge out 46,000 match Nonmajor in 40,000 (15,000 E911 + 25,000 Parks) and Road Sinking in 46,000; no hidden transfers inside spending lines. Read pages 1-12 of 12"
}